From efdc34f1761332aa4c198c4bea04c667785e93c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:57:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/57] nouveau/vk: put block-linear mappings in the big-page
 half on Horizon
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A non-pitch PTE kind is block-linear, and the GPU MMU only fills
block-linear kinds in big pages on Maxwell: such a mapping in the
small-page half faults on first access rather than failing to map. NVK
asks for one whenever an image's layout is tiled — nvk_image.c passes
plane->nil.pte_kind straight through — and does not necessarily round
the size to a big page, so choosing the half by size and alignment
alone put some tiled images in the wrong one.

Found by reading the paths the first hardware run will take. It is the
shape of bug that does not fail at the call that causes it: the map
succeeds and the fault arrives later, somewhere else.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 4 — reducing avoidable first-run failures
---
 .../vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c    | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c
index 8e6bc1c..a163256 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c
@@ -221,6 +221,24 @@ nvkmd_horizon_alloc_va(struct nvkmd_dev *_dev,
        (size_B % big) == 0 && (align_B % big) == 0)
       page_size = big;
 
+   /* A non-pitch PTE kind is block-linear, and the GPU MMU only fills
+    * block-linear kinds in big pages on Maxwell: a block-linear mapping
+    * in the small-page half faults on first access rather than failing
+    * to map. NVK asks for such a kind whenever an image's layout is
+    * tiled (nvk_image.c:1175 passes plane->nil.pte_kind straight
+    * through), and it does not necessarily round the size to a big
+    * page, so the rule above alone would put some tiled images in the
+    * wrong half.
+    *
+    * Where the kind demands it, the big-page half is taken and the size
+    * rounded up to match — horizon_gpu_vm_reserve rounds to page_size
+    * itself, so this only has to choose the half. Refusing instead
+    * would fail a legal request; mapping it in the small-page half
+    * would be the silent wrong answer.
+    */
+   if (pte_kind != HORIZON_GPU_PTE_KIND_PITCH && big != 0)
+      page_size = big;
+
    horizon_gpu_result res =
       horizon_gpu_vm_reserve(dev->gpu, size_B, page_size, align_B,
                              &va->range);
-- 
